      "question": {
        ":question/id": "31d5493d-598a-5cd3-9717-dec41584eaba",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate $det(Z)$, if\n $Z=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{x} & y \\\\ {y}^{2} & \\sqrt{x}\\end{bmatrix}.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(Z) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x} & y \\\\ {y}^{2} & \\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{x}-y\\cdot {y}^{2} \\\\  & =x-{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
